1
00:00:11,740 --> 00:00:12,700
Taro.

2
00:00:12,990 --> 00:00:14,280
Good morning, Dad.

3
00:00:14,450 --> 00:00:16,780
Breakfast is almost ready.

4
00:00:17,450 --> 00:00:20,160
I've decided to return to Japan.

5
00:00:22,710 --> 00:00:23,960
Japan!?

6
00:00:24,790 --> 00:00:26,460
Paris, September.

7
00:00:26,960 --> 00:00:30,420
Almost one month has passed since the first National Youth Tournament in France...

8
00:00:30,550 --> 00:00:32,970
...has gone by.

9
00:00:33,970 --> 00:00:35,090
For the Japan youth team...

10
00:00:35,180 --> 00:00:40,430
...you said this when you were trying to decide to play.

11
00:00:40,890 --> 00:00:44,480
It's better to take action than to regret, isn't it?

12
00:00:45,390 --> 00:00:46,190
Yes.

13
00:00:46,690 --> 00:00:50,110
The way you worked hard inspired me.

14
00:00:50,190 --> 00:00:55,070
I want to paint one more picture of Mount Fuji.

15
00:00:55,450 --> 00:00:57,410
I'm encouraging you, Dad.

16
00:00:57,910 --> 00:01:04,000
I may not be able to paint Mount Fuji as I imagined yet...

17
00:01:04,500 --> 00:01:09,710
...but it's better to try and fail, right?

18
00:01:12,130 --> 00:01:13,050
Yes!

19
00:01:25,350 --> 00:01:30,270
CAPTAIN TSUBASA: JUNIOR YOUTH ARC

20
00:02:44,510 --> 00:02:48,230
Episode 38
Towards a New Era

21
00:02:44,970 --> 00:02:48,230
We are at the final of the first-year autumn tournament in Shizuoka.

22
00:02:48,310 --> 00:02:51,440
First-Year Tournament Final: Nankatsu Middle School - Otomo Middle School

23
00:02:48,520 --> 00:02:53,020
We are in the second half, and Nankatsu is 0-0 against Otomo.

24
00:02:53,110 --> 00:02:56,360
My watch says we are at the 30th minute.

25
00:02:56,650 --> 00:02:59,610
And now only extra time minutes remain.

26
00:02:59,900 --> 00:03:02,700
Are we going into extra time?

27
00:03:07,290 --> 00:03:12,540
Oh, and in this chaos, Otomo captain Nitta takes possession of the ball.

28
00:03:12,620 --> 00:03:14,790
Great, go, Nitta!

29
00:03:15,130 --> 00:03:17,300
Defend, boys.

30
00:03:20,800 --> 00:03:22,800
Falcon Shot!

31
00:03:27,560 --> 00:03:31,770
Goal! Finally, Otomo scores the first goal!

32
00:03:34,100 --> 00:03:37,070
And dear viewers, this is the end of the game.

33
00:03:37,690 --> 00:03:39,530
We did it! We won!

34
00:03:39,610 --> 00:03:41,780
We beat Nankatsu!

35
00:03:41,900 --> 00:03:43,320
Hooray!

36
00:03:43,410 --> 00:03:47,120
Otomo Middle School wins 1-0!

37
00:03:47,280 --> 00:03:50,580
They prevented Nankatsu Middle School's 4th championship.

38
00:03:50,870 --> 00:03:53,750
Nitta did it!

39
00:03:55,380 --> 00:04:00,260
And with this, Nankatsu's three-year consecutive victory...

40
00:04:00,340 --> 00:04:03,010
...officially comes to an end.

41
00:04:05,430 --> 00:04:07,470
We lost in the end.

42
00:04:07,550 --> 00:04:11,060
I guess without you guys, nothing is as it used to be.

43
00:04:13,480 --> 00:04:14,730
Hyuga!

44
00:04:15,440 --> 00:04:19,360
Whether it's Otomo Middle School or Nankatsu Middle School, it doesn't matter.

45
00:04:19,650 --> 00:04:24,700
Be at ease. This year, Toho Academy Middle School, led by Takeshi...

46
00:04:24,780 --> 00:04:28,240
...will win the second National Middle School Championship this year.

47
00:04:29,870 --> 00:04:34,870
And likewise, we will make Toho Academy High School champions.

48
00:04:36,960 --> 00:04:41,050
Wakashimazu and I are training at high school now.

49
00:04:41,170 --> 00:04:45,430
And of course, we aim to be in the main squad next spring.

50
00:04:46,800 --> 00:04:50,390
We are all going to Nankatsu High School!

51
00:04:50,470 --> 00:04:53,640
We will beat Toho again.

52
00:04:55,060 --> 00:04:58,150
See you next winter at the high school tournament.

53
00:04:58,770 --> 00:05:00,020
See you later.

54
00:05:00,190 --> 00:05:02,780
Wait, aren't you going to say hello to Tsubasa?

55
00:05:06,820 --> 00:05:08,950
Tsubasa is going to Brazil.

56
00:05:09,490 --> 00:05:13,660
We shared the middle school senior championship.

57
00:05:13,950 --> 00:05:18,630
Until you return, I won't give the title of Japan's number one to anyone.

58
00:05:19,750 --> 00:05:21,960
So go to Brazil quickly and become a professional.

59
00:05:22,300 --> 00:05:27,760
Next time we meet, we'll be in the Japan National Team again.

60
00:05:28,680 --> 00:05:32,310
Don't cry, boys. You did your best.

61
00:05:33,020 --> 00:05:36,810
But... we... the record of you senpais...

62
00:05:37,310 --> 00:05:39,770
Records are made to be broken.

63
00:05:39,900 --> 00:05:46,320
Use this disappointment and train harder tomorrow.

64
00:05:47,490 --> 00:05:48,820
Okay!

65
00:05:50,950 --> 00:05:53,620
Oh, so Hyuga was there.

66
00:05:53,910 --> 00:05:58,830
We retired, but that doesn't mean we can't go to a training session.

67
00:05:59,630 --> 00:06:04,250
If we don't, then Hyuga and his team will become completely better than us.

68
00:06:04,340 --> 00:06:05,590
You're right.

69
00:06:05,840 --> 00:06:09,340
Same for me. Can I entrust the lower grades to you while I'm gone?

70
00:06:09,760 --> 00:06:10,590
What?

71
00:06:11,350 --> 00:06:14,180
Yes. Katagiri-san recommended me to Hamana's senior team.

72
00:06:14,260 --> 00:06:18,600
Starting tomorrow, I'll be training with them.

73
00:06:18,850 --> 00:06:21,400
What!? That Hamana!?

74
00:06:21,480 --> 00:06:23,440
- Yes. - That's great!

75
00:06:23,520 --> 00:06:27,110
Congratulations. I'm sure you'll fit in with them.

76
00:06:27,320 --> 00:06:29,950
Yes, thank you, guys.

77
00:06:30,610 --> 00:06:33,620
Hamburg.

78
00:06:40,540 --> 00:06:42,130
Hey, great!

79
00:06:47,260 --> 00:06:49,760
I swore to the Japan team.

80
00:06:49,970 --> 00:06:53,180
I won't return home until I become a professional.

81
00:06:53,850 --> 00:06:56,640
Wakabayashi, they're calling from the office.

82
00:06:57,730 --> 00:06:58,680
Okay.

83
00:07:01,310 --> 00:07:03,060
Hello. This is Wakabayashi.

84
00:07:05,610 --> 00:07:06,530
What?

85
00:07:06,610 --> 00:07:08,070
A professional contract!?

86
00:07:08,440 --> 00:07:11,860
Our main goalkeeper Mike got injured.

87
00:07:11,950 --> 00:07:14,330
The doctor says it will take 6 months to recover.

88
00:07:15,120 --> 00:07:18,750
So we need a new goalkeeper.

89
00:07:19,080 --> 00:07:22,210
I want to sign a professional contract with you immediately.

90
00:07:23,790 --> 00:07:28,170
The board of directors, regarding protecting Hamburg's goal...

91
00:07:28,260 --> 00:07:32,130
...has long considered you the only person who can do this job.

92
00:07:32,300 --> 00:07:35,600
This is a golden opportunity.

93
00:07:35,850 --> 00:07:38,810
I didn't think you would value me this much.

94
00:07:38,890 --> 00:07:41,600
Of course, my answer is yes.

95
00:07:43,440 --> 00:07:46,690
But I have one request.

96
00:07:46,770 --> 00:07:47,610
What?

97
00:07:47,820 --> 00:07:54,780
While living in Germany, I still want to be able to play for Japan.

98
00:07:55,450 --> 00:07:58,790
It may seem absurd to you, but my dream...

99
00:07:58,870 --> 00:08:03,460
...is to be the goalkeeper of the team when Japan becomes world champion.

100
00:08:05,710 --> 00:08:08,710
Above all, I want to sign as a Japanese player.

101
00:08:08,800 --> 00:08:15,220
And if an opportunity to play for Japan arises, I want to prioritize it.

102
00:08:15,930 --> 00:08:20,390
I promised my Japanese teammates.

103
00:08:25,270 --> 00:08:26,110
So...

104
00:08:26,190 --> 00:08:27,020
How fast!

105
00:08:31,900 --> 00:08:34,360
This is incredible!

106
00:08:35,780 --> 00:08:37,870
What do you think about Tsubasa?

107
00:08:37,950 --> 00:08:41,660
I would very much like him to play for us.

108
00:08:42,040 --> 00:08:45,000
He may not have physical strength, but...

109
00:08:45,000 --> 00:08:48,670
...he compensates for it with his technique and speed.

110
00:08:49,170 --> 00:08:52,920
Most importantly, his ball control is exceptional.

111
00:08:53,050 --> 00:08:53,970
Yes.

112
00:08:54,050 --> 00:08:58,220
When he grows up and further develops his skills in Brazil...

113
00:08:58,300 --> 00:09:03,560
...he will undoubtedly carry the Japan team to the top.

114
00:09:04,850 --> 00:09:10,320
Just as I thought, Tsubasa now has the skills of a professional.

115
00:09:11,030 --> 00:09:13,440
I think it's time to make my offer.

116
00:09:19,160 --> 00:09:23,580
Tsubasa's training with Hamana continued.

117
00:09:23,950 --> 00:09:25,960
Paris.

118
00:09:26,170 --> 00:09:28,960
Thank you for coming to see me off, guys.

119
00:09:29,420 --> 00:09:31,880
Misaki-kun, this is from all of us.

120
00:09:32,710 --> 00:09:37,720
We weren't sure what to get, but we thought this would be better.

121
00:09:37,930 --> 00:09:41,140
A football and training equipment.

122
00:09:41,720 --> 00:09:42,970
Thank you.

123
00:09:43,680 --> 00:09:45,100
Take care of yourself, okay?

124
00:09:45,180 --> 00:09:49,270
You too, keep training in Japan, okay, Misaki-kun?

125
00:09:49,900 --> 00:09:50,770
Okay.

126
00:09:53,900 --> 00:09:56,990
No matter how many times you change schools...

127
00:09:57,400 --> 00:09:59,530
...saying goodbye is always hard.

128
00:10:00,370 --> 00:10:01,200
Yes.

129
00:10:05,910 --> 00:10:09,170
Misaki really left.

130
00:10:10,630 --> 00:10:15,090
Goodbye, Misaki-kun. I'll always support you.

131
00:10:16,630 --> 00:10:17,510
Guys.

132
00:10:17,800 --> 00:10:19,760
Bomb news!

133
00:10:20,340 --> 00:10:21,550
You mean this?

134
00:10:21,640 --> 00:10:23,600
Unexpected Professional Contract for 15-year-old Genzo Wakabayashi

135
00:10:21,760 --> 00:10:23,600
Oh, you knew?

136
00:10:23,680 --> 00:10:26,640
Of course. We're ahead of you.

137
00:10:26,810 --> 00:10:27,640
Good morning.

138
00:10:27,730 --> 00:10:29,980
Tsubasa, have you seen the news?

139
00:10:30,060 --> 00:10:30,900
Yes.

140
00:10:31,190 --> 00:10:33,730
You finally made it, Wakabayashi-kun.

141
00:10:34,070 --> 00:10:36,190
You surpassed me.

142
00:10:36,900 --> 00:10:39,320
Japan Football Federation.

143
00:10:39,410 --> 00:10:43,910
Japan Team Player Selection Meeting

144
00:10:39,820 --> 00:10:40,820
What!?

145
00:10:40,910 --> 00:10:43,910
Now you want Ozora Tsubasa to become a member of the national team?

146
00:10:44,240 --> 00:10:47,410
It's too early, Katagiri-san.

147
00:10:47,620 --> 00:10:52,420
Of course, this would attract some public attention...

148
00:10:52,580 --> 00:10:57,420
...but he doesn't yet have the physical conditions to compete at the world level.

149
00:10:57,800 --> 00:11:00,470
And foreign players are very big-bodied.

150
00:11:00,550 --> 00:11:04,050
If he suffers a serious injury, it would be a disadvantage for us.

151
00:11:04,350 --> 00:11:08,390
Why don't we wait a bit for him to develop himself first?

152
00:11:08,480 --> 00:11:10,270
We can't wait that long.

153
00:11:11,190 --> 00:11:15,820
Ozora Tsubasa will completely change Japanese football!

154
00:11:18,320 --> 00:11:20,200
Wakabayashi did it!

155
00:11:20,450 --> 00:11:22,530
Are you excited, Tsubasa-kun?

156
00:11:22,610 --> 00:11:26,700
Yes, I'm eagerly looking forward to the day when I play a match against Wakabayashi-kun.

157
00:11:26,950 --> 00:11:30,500
Maybe they also call him "Super Goalkeeper" in Germany.

158
00:11:32,460 --> 00:11:34,920
Alright, take your places.

159
00:11:35,920 --> 00:11:39,340
I start today by introducing our transfer student.

160
00:11:40,630 --> 00:11:42,260
Alright, come in.

161
00:11:49,020 --> 00:11:50,730
Wh- What!?

162
00:11:51,060 --> 00:11:52,480
Misaki-kun!

163
00:11:52,980 --> 00:11:58,030
Hello. I'm happy to be at Nankatsu Middle School. I'm Misaki Taro.

164
00:11:58,230 --> 00:12:00,360
CAPTAIN TSUBASA: JUNIOR YOUTH ARC

165
00:12:02,700 --> 00:12:04,990
Hamburg Team | Born: December 7 | Blood Type: O

166
00:12:05,530 --> 00:12:08,240
Welcome, Misaki!

167
00:12:08,540 --> 00:12:09,540
Since you're here...

168
00:12:09,660 --> 00:12:12,670
Since you're here, we can play on equal terms with Hyuga and Toho!

169
00:12:12,710 --> 00:12:14,250
Equal terms?

170
00:12:14,920 --> 00:12:15,790
That's right.

171
00:12:15,880 --> 00:12:18,340
Tsubasa-kun, after you graduate from middle school...

172
00:12:18,420 --> 00:12:21,010
...you'll go to Brazil to see Roberto.

173
00:12:21,220 --> 00:12:22,050
Yes.

174
00:12:22,220 --> 00:12:26,640
It seems I won't be able to play with you in high school then.

175
00:12:28,430 --> 00:12:31,230
But I know that as long as we continue playing football...

176
00:12:31,270 --> 00:12:33,640
...one day we will definitely reestablish our unity.

177
00:12:33,890 --> 00:12:34,940
Tsubasa-kun?

178
00:12:35,060 --> 00:12:37,020
Yes, of course.

179
00:12:42,150 --> 00:12:43,400
As time passed...

180
00:12:44,950 --> 00:12:51,160
While Tsubasa spent his days with the Hamana club and his Portuguese...

181
00:12:46,870 --> 00:12:48,370
Proper Brazilian Portuguese Learning

182
00:12:53,370 --> 00:12:58,500
Former teammates and rivals who once played for the Japan youth team...

183
00:12:58,590 --> 00:13:04,470
...each worked hard in line with the goals they set for themselves.

184
00:13:00,170 --> 00:13:02,170
Tatsunami High School Admission Request

185
00:13:05,050 --> 00:13:07,640
Is that so! Really, with Tsubasa...

186
00:13:07,850 --> 00:13:10,100
I'm very happy for you, Sanae-chan!

187
00:13:10,220 --> 00:13:13,680
Yes, thank you. How is Misugi-kun?

188
00:13:14,140 --> 00:13:19,190
Jun is trying to get into a high school affiliated with a medical school.

189
00:13:19,320 --> 00:13:22,190
Wow, so he wants to become a doctor?

190
00:13:22,480 --> 00:13:25,900
But he says he still wants to continue with football.

191
00:13:26,110 --> 00:13:29,870
Apparently, he heard about a Brazilian footballer named Socrates...

192
00:13:29,990 --> 00:13:32,950
...who could be both a doctor and a footballer.

193
00:13:33,040 --> 00:13:36,670
Jun is working hard to be like him.

194
00:13:37,170 --> 00:13:39,710
Furano Middle School, Hokkaido

195
00:13:44,010 --> 00:13:45,220
Fujisawa.

196
00:13:45,470 --> 00:13:47,590
I haven't seen you for a long time, Matsuyama-kun.

197
00:13:47,930 --> 00:13:50,600
What a surprise! What are you doing here?

198
00:13:50,800 --> 00:13:54,520
My father's work is finishing earlier than I expected.

199
00:13:54,680 --> 00:13:58,600
He thought I needed to take an exam for a Japanese high school.

200
00:13:58,810 --> 00:14:02,190
So I also returned earlier.

201
00:14:02,400 --> 00:14:05,610
Is that so? So where do you want to go?

202
00:14:05,990 --> 00:14:07,400
Furano High School.

203
00:14:07,450 --> 00:14:08,780
Me too.

204
00:14:10,620 --> 00:14:15,750
If we both get in, will you be the team captain again and stay by my side?

205
00:14:16,120 --> 00:14:18,210
Yes, of course.

206
00:14:21,630 --> 00:14:25,630
And here, at Toho Academy High School...

207
00:14:34,310 --> 00:14:37,560
Hyuga, Wakashimazu, and Sorimachi...

208
00:14:37,640 --> 00:14:41,810
...are expected to become the main members of the team as soon as they start high school.

209
00:14:42,560 --> 00:14:48,450
When they get through the exam season, fierce battles will begin again.

210
00:14:49,530 --> 00:14:51,530
Japan Player Selection Final Meeting

211
00:14:51,870 --> 00:14:55,080
Gentlemen, as soon as he graduates from middle school...

212
00:14:55,200 --> 00:14:58,250
...Tsubasa is going to Brazil to become a professional.

213
00:14:58,710 --> 00:15:04,710
Before he goes, I want to do the best we can for him.

214
00:15:04,800 --> 00:15:07,760
Unexpected Professional Contract for 15-year-old Genzo Wakabayashi

215
00:15:05,050 --> 00:15:09,800
Genzo Wakabayashi, just like Tsubasa, is a 15-year-old professional player in Germany.

216
00:15:10,220 --> 00:15:14,300
This is the generation we were expecting.

217
00:15:17,600 --> 00:15:22,900
Katagiri-kun, as the technical committee stated, now is not the time.

218
00:15:23,020 --> 00:15:24,230
Sir.

219
00:15:24,520 --> 00:15:28,940
He is young and talented, and he is now going to Brazil.

220
00:15:29,240 --> 00:15:32,070
I don't understand this rush.

221
00:15:34,370 --> 00:15:36,910
I watched his game.

222
00:15:37,040 --> 00:15:39,910
I know he will become a great player.

223
00:15:40,210 --> 00:15:43,880
And that is why we must raise him carefully.

224
00:15:46,800 --> 00:15:50,340
The next day, a list was announced for the Japan team.

225
00:15:50,670 --> 00:15:57,430
Two players from Hamana, where Tsubasa trained, were selected.

226
00:15:58,020 --> 00:16:03,190
Tsubasa, I tried hard for you, but I couldn't get you into the national team.

227
00:16:03,310 --> 00:16:07,820
What? Impossible. I can't do this.

228
00:16:07,980 --> 00:16:10,860
Never say those words again.

229
00:16:12,360 --> 00:16:16,620
I don't want to hear you say "I can't" or anything like that ever again.

230
00:16:18,740 --> 00:16:23,080
I supported you to get into the Japan team because I believe in your talent.

231
00:16:23,290 --> 00:16:26,540
I want you to always aim for the best.

232
00:16:27,090 --> 00:16:29,050
Even after you go to Brazil and become a professional...

233
00:16:29,170 --> 00:16:33,840
...keep striving, and let your target there be to become the number one professional.

234
00:16:34,260 --> 00:16:38,010
I want you to be the best footballer in the whole world.

235
00:16:45,190 --> 00:16:49,440
In my playing days, I had to quit football because of injury.

236
00:16:49,820 --> 00:16:52,110
You are living my dream.

237
00:16:55,110 --> 00:16:57,370
I know you are also living Roberto's dream.

238
00:16:57,620 --> 00:17:00,450
On behalf of all Japanese fans in the world...

239
00:17:00,540 --> 00:17:04,790
...the fans who want you to direct the future of Japanese football...

240
00:17:06,380 --> 00:17:08,210
You are living their dream!

241
00:17:12,420 --> 00:17:14,050
Japan Team.

242
00:17:19,930 --> 00:17:24,980
All the games they played had an age limit.

243
00:17:25,770 --> 00:17:30,770
But not anymore. That was my previous football life.

244
00:17:31,320 --> 00:17:36,660
I want to fight to be the best in Japan and the best in the world!

245
00:17:37,820 --> 00:17:43,540
And if I'm going to Brazil to become a professional, I have to be number one.

246
00:17:44,000 --> 00:17:46,790
Japan Training Camp - Shizuoka

247
00:17:46,920 --> 00:17:50,250
That day, a friendly match was planned between the newly formed Japan team...

248
00:17:50,340 --> 00:17:54,880
...and a local university team.

249
00:17:58,050 --> 00:18:02,140
Today, I want to take an entrance exam a little earlier than everyone else.

250
00:18:02,510 --> 00:18:04,350
An entrance exam for the Japan team.

251
00:18:04,930 --> 00:18:07,190
No one made this decision for me.

252
00:18:08,060 --> 00:18:09,900
This is my own struggle.

253
00:18:10,860 --> 00:18:11,690
Get ready!

254
00:18:15,740 --> 00:18:17,200
Pass the ball to the goalkeeper.

255
00:18:17,610 --> 00:18:18,410
Okay!

256
00:18:19,660 --> 00:18:20,570
What?

257
00:18:21,080 --> 00:18:22,410
Alright, go at them!

258
00:18:22,530 --> 00:18:24,790
I'm going to the Japan goal!

259
00:18:24,910 --> 00:18:27,000
- Tsubasa! - This...

260
00:18:27,210 --> 00:18:30,580
What are you doing? Cut him off, crush him!

261
00:18:30,790 --> 00:18:32,090
O- Okay, coach.

262
00:18:37,470 --> 00:18:38,430
What!?

263
00:18:42,510 --> 00:18:43,430
Impossible!

264
00:18:43,510 --> 00:18:44,810
Who is this kid!?

265
00:18:46,770 --> 00:18:47,850
Two more...

266
00:18:56,030 --> 00:18:57,240
Good. I did it!

267
00:18:57,320 --> 00:18:59,320
I got past the last defense!

268
00:19:01,410 --> 00:19:02,450
Coach!

269
00:19:04,200 --> 00:19:05,910
He's the coach of the Japan team!

270
00:19:06,250 --> 00:19:08,710
Okay. I'll get past him and shoot!

271
00:19:10,670 --> 00:19:12,460
I am Ozora Tsubasa!

272
00:19:12,580 --> 00:19:15,960
The one who will make Japanese football number one in the world!

273
00:19:17,970 --> 00:19:19,090
Tsubasa!

274
00:19:23,350 --> 00:19:26,560
It was impressive. That move anticipated Tsubasa.

275
00:19:26,890 --> 00:19:33,560
Not surprising. He traveled around Europe as a professional and won.

276
00:19:38,190 --> 00:19:39,900
In the end, it was useless.

277
00:19:40,200 --> 00:19:41,910
I lost.

278
00:19:46,790 --> 00:19:50,620
Friends, my behavior was selfish!

279
00:19:50,960 --> 00:19:52,170
Forgive me.

280
00:19:53,960 --> 00:19:55,210
It won't happen again.

281
00:19:59,760 --> 00:20:00,630
Wait.

282
00:20:03,260 --> 00:20:06,600
Would you like to play a little more with these kids?

283
00:20:08,310 --> 00:20:12,440
You can play for the Japan team.

284
00:20:12,690 --> 00:20:16,110
Your dribbles were breathtaking, Ozora Tsubasa-kun.

285
00:20:18,150 --> 00:20:19,440
Coach.

286
00:20:27,700 --> 00:20:31,410
Tsubasa is absent again today.

287
00:20:31,620 --> 00:20:32,920
Any news from him?

288
00:20:32,960 --> 00:20:36,790
No. He also didn't contact the manager.

289
00:20:36,880 --> 00:20:37,960
Hey, look!

290
00:20:38,050 --> 00:20:38,920
What?

291
00:20:39,300 --> 00:20:40,300
Look!

292
00:20:40,420 --> 00:20:43,130
15-Year-Old Ozora Tsubasa Joined the Japan Team!

293
00:20:40,760 --> 00:20:43,130
Tsubasa in the Japan team!?

294
00:20:43,220 --> 00:20:45,090
He created a miracle!

295
00:20:43,220 --> 00:20:45,090
The Birth of the Future Youngest Asian Star of Japanese Football with a Historic Selection

296
00:20:45,640 --> 00:20:47,470
Did you see it too?

297
00:20:47,550 --> 00:20:49,560
We just saw it now.

298
00:20:49,810 --> 00:20:53,560
That's Tsubasa. He doesn't miss any opportunity.

299
00:20:53,690 --> 00:20:55,650
There's one more news!

300
00:20:55,770 --> 00:21:00,280
The Japan team will play its first national match against Paraguay.

301
00:21:00,860 --> 00:21:02,490
Paraguay?

302
00:21:02,610 --> 00:21:04,320
I wonder if Tsubasa will play?

303
00:21:05,990 --> 00:21:07,780
Of course he will play.

304
00:21:10,910 --> 00:21:13,330
We can't play around anymore!

305
00:21:13,410 --> 00:21:18,130
Let's follow Tsubasa's path and pass our entrance exam!

306
00:21:18,590 --> 00:21:20,880
The news of Tsubasa joining the national team...

307
00:21:20,960 --> 00:21:24,720
...spread quickly among his teammates all over Japan!

308
00:21:27,300 --> 00:21:29,850
The boy finally did it!

309
00:21:34,350 --> 00:21:37,770
Luckily I got into the team.

310
00:21:38,360 --> 00:21:43,490
Now I just have to do my best for the coach who believed in me.

311
00:21:44,240 --> 00:21:49,070
I have to bring out all the talents I have.

312
00:21:53,000 --> 00:21:55,000
My goal is to be number one in the world!

313
00:21:55,620 --> 00:21:56,920
Go!

314
00:21:58,040 --> 00:22:01,250
This is Tsubasa's special shot, the Drive Shot.

315
00:22:03,380 --> 00:22:07,300
I will be the number one player in the world!

316
00:24:46,290 --> 00:24:50,030
NEXT EPISODE
TSUBASA TAKES OFF